Add a request timeout for the Keystone and service clients

Horizon has no request-timeout setting.
`openstack_auth.utils.get_session` builds the keystoneauth session of
every login and token request with
`session.Session(verify=verify, **kwargs)`, and the dashboard builds the
Keystone session of `keystoneclient`
(openstack_dashboard/api/keystone.py), the Placement session of
`make_adapter` (api/placement.py), the session of `networkclient` and
the neutronclient of `neutronclient` (api/neutron.py), the novaclient of
`cached_novaclient` (api/_nova.py), the cinderclient of `cinderclient`
(api/cinder.py) and the glanceclient of `glanceclient` (api/glance.py)
without a timeout. glanceclient falls back to its own 600 seconds, every
other client to none. A service that stops answering on an established
connection holds the uWSGI process that serves the page until the kernel
gives up on the connection (`tcp_retries2 = 15`, about 15.6 minutes),
long after the gateway in front of the dashboard answered the browser
with 503 or 504 (#1799).

The patch adds the setting `OPENSTACK_REQUEST_TIMEOUT`, `None` by
default, to openstack_auth/defaults.py and
openstack_dashboard/defaults.py beside `OPENSTACK_SSL_NO_VERIFY`.
`get_session` passes it as `timeout` unless the caller gave one, and
every session and client constructor named above passes it as `timeout`.
glanceclient turns its timeout into a float and takes no `None`, so the
Glance client gets the argument only when the setting is not `None`.
With the setting at `None`, every constructor behaves as upstream. The
horizon-operator renders `OPENSTACK_REQUEST_TIMEOUT = 30`: Horizon's
sessions pass no retries, so a hung call ends after 30 seconds and the
user sees Horizon's own error.

Tests: no upstream test pins the arguments of these constructors. The
patch adds GetSessionTimeoutTestCase to
openstack_auth/tests/unit/test_utils.py and one test class per client
module under openstack_dashboard/test/unit/api/ (test_keystone.py,
test_cinder.py, test_glance.py, test_neutron.py (networkclient and
neutronclient), test_nova.py, and a new test_placement.py), each with
the setting at 7 and at `None`. Without the code hunks 13 of the 14
dashboard tests and the get_session test fail; the Glance test with the
setting at `None` asserts that no `timeout` argument is passed, which
holds upstream too.

Proof: test_request_timeout_reaches_every_client in
tests/container-images/verify_horizon.sh sets
`OPENSTACK_REQUEST_TIMEOUT = 7` in the built image and asserts the
`timeout` of `get_session()` and of every patched constructor, then
repeats with `None` and asserts that the Glance client gets no `timeout`
argument.

The 2026.2 twin carries the same change cut from 27.0.0: 27.0.0 dropped
neutronclient and added a second Nova session, `computeclient`.

Applies to horizon 25.7.0 (2026.1).

Upstream status: not yet proposed.
